Author: Lukáš Lalinský <lukas@lalinsky.com>
Date:   Fri Feb 6 09:43:37 2026 +0100

    Fix NetBSD test failures (#290)

    Three test failures were fixed for NetBSD:

    1. Pipe error normalization (kqueue backend):
       - BSD systems return EBADF (NotOpenForWriting) when writing to closed pipes
       - Normalize to BrokenPipe in kqueue backend for consistency with Linux
       - Handles both kqueue event errors and writev errors

    2. Socket buffer size test (net.zig):
       - Reduced buffer sizes from 128KB/256KB to 32KB/64KB for all platforms
       - More conservative sizes avoid hitting platform-specific resource limits

    3. Event synchronization tests (os/thread_wait.zig):
       - Fixed Event creation to happen on the waiting thread (required for
         NetBSD's lwp_park/lwp_unpark implementation)
       - Added loop in timeout test to handle spurious wakeups from stale
         EALREADY errors caused by per-thread unpark flag interference
         between tests

    All changes maintain compatibility with Linux and other platforms.

