commit 70a1a22c960070fbf138d419ceea79df38805248
Author: Lukas Lalinsky <lukas@lalinsky.com>
Date:   Sat Jun 27 12:51:33 2026 +0200

    ev/thread_pool: drain queued work in stop()

    After stop() joins the workers, items submitted but never picked up can
    remain linked in the queue. A later cancel() could remove one and invoke
    its completion_fn (waking a loop being torn down), breaking the
    "no callback after stop" invariant. Drain the queue under the lock so
    this can't happen and the documented "drop any queued work" holds.

